# Copy to .env (beside this file, at the top of the repository) and point it at
# your own dump. .devcontainer/docker-compose.yml reads it to know what to mount.
#
# This project ships no game data. Translations are generated locally from the
# dump you supply, so a container with nothing mounted can build the runtime and
# synthetic tests and cannot verify anything against the original program.
#
# Quote any value with a space in it. Compose strips the quotes; a shell
# sourcing this file needs them.
#
# The dump is mounted at this same path inside the container, and post-create.sh
# links `Haunting Ground (USA)` at the top of the workspace to it.
#
# .env is gitignored. Do not commit paths from your own machine.

# The directory holding SLUS_210.75, DATA.CVM and MODULES/.
HG_GAME_DIR="/home/you/Games/Haunting Ground (USA)"

# ro (the default) or rw. The dump is an input; nothing should write to it.
HG_MOUNT_MODE=ro

# Only set these if the desktop sockets are somewhere other than the default.
#XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000
#WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0